CORE
main.cpp
--pointer-check
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ inserted: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
dead object in .*: FAILURE$
--
elide_cpp_returned_temporaries inserted the DECL of the ignored result's
slot before the call with insert_before, so the do-while's jump back to the
call skipped it, and the DEAD after the first call ended its lifetime for
the following ones.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails
only its WRONG assertion.
